Third-party material
--------------------------------------------------------------------------

This repository is a component and an example application. It does not
vendor its dependencies; it is built against them.

  Matter SDK (project-chip/connectedhomeip)   Apache-2.0
  Zephyr RTOS                                 Apache-2.0
  OpenThread                                  BSD-3-Clause
  nRF Connect SDK (nrfconnect/sdk-nrf)        LicenseRef-Nordic-5-Clause
  nRF Door Lock and Access Control Add-on     LicenseRef-Nordic-5-Clause

`examples/lock/` and `examples/light_bulb/` derive their Kconfig, board and
sysbuild files from Nordic Semiconductor sample configuration and retain
Nordic's SPDX headers and copyright where the original text survives. Those
files remain under LicenseRef-Nordic-5-Clause, which permits use with Nordic
Semiconductor integrated circuits.

Everything under `lib/tunnel/`, `zap/VendorTunnelCluster.xml`,
`zap/add_tunnel_cluster.py`, `measure/` and `tools/` is original work by the
copyright holder and is Apache-2.0.

The example applications compile the upstream application's sources *in place*
rather than copying them. The single exception is
`examples/light_bulb/src/chip_project_config.h`, a ten-line build configuration
header copied verbatim from the nRF Connect SDK light bulb sample with its
Nordic header intact, because the build resolves that path relative to the
application directory. No Nordic application logic is redistributed here.
Obtain the upstream applications from:

  https://github.com/nrfconnect/ncs-door-lock-and-access-control
  https://github.com/nrfconnect/sdk-nrf  (samples/matter/light_bulb)

Device attestation certificates under `evidence/test-vectors/` are Matter
*test* credentials (VID 0xFFF1) from the public Matter SDK development PKI.
They are not production credentials and confer no attestation of conformance.
